  "notes": "ETYMOLOGY:\n{借|かり} (borrow) + {入|いれ} (in/receive) - receiving borrowed funds\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {貸出|かしだ}し - lending\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {借入|かりいれ}する - to borrow\n- {借入金|かりいれきん} - borrowed money, loan\n- {借入|かりいれ}{残高|ざんだか} - outstanding loan balance\n- {借入|かりいれ}{期間|きかん} - loan period\n- {借入|かりいれ}{限度額|げんどがく} - borrowing limit\n- {借入|かりいれ}{利率|りりつ} - borrowing interest rate\n- {短期|たんき}{借入|かりいれ} - short-term borrowing\n- {長期|ちょうき}{借入|かりいれ} - long-term borrowing\n\nRELATED FINANCIAL TERMS:\n- {融資|ゆうし} - financing, loan (from lender's perspective)\n- ローン - loan (loanword)\n- {返済|へんさい} - repayment\n- {利息|りそく} - interest\n- {担保|たんぽ} - collateral\n\nUSAGE:\nPrimarily used in financial and business contexts. For casual borrowing (like borrowing a book), use {借|か}りる instead.",
